  <item nodeId="node-0x56165fcfeaf0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Ozymandias
Two vast and trunkless legs of stone stand in the desert. Near them on the sand, half sunk, a shattered visage lies. The legs are atop a pedestal.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>YES</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56165fdbf640"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56165fdbf640">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at legs</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Vast stone legs extend upwards, but whatever torso once existed atop them is long gone now, obliterated by the cruel passage of endless ages.Atop the left leg, resplendent in its glory, sits the kingfisher. Atop the right leg, tiny but audacious, sits the goldcrest.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>YES</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56165e3f15c0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You head through the huge iron doors into the tunnel beyond. Eventually the tunnel opens out into what appears to be an arena.

You push against the enormous rusted iron door with all your might, but it will not budge. There must be some way to open it.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56165f47af30"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56165f47af30">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x door</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Vast and unyielding and impossibly ancient, you wonder who could have built this enormous portal. The doors must weigh hundreds of tons; they are covered in thick red rust but you detect no signs of corrosion or structural weakness.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56165f1f83c0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56165f1f83c0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">e</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">
Ozymandias
Two vast and trunkless legs of stone stand in the desert. Near them on the sand, half sunk, a shattered visage lies. The legs are atop a pedestal.

You can see a weasel here.

&gt;</result>
